<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      Make the tenant_isolation policy answer, rather than throw, on a connection with no tenant.

      `current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid` casts the raw GUC. The GUC's "no
      tenant" value is the EMPTY STRING — that is what TenantAwareDataSource writes on every
      tenantless checkout and on every connection reset at close — and ''::uuid raises
      "invalid input syntax for type uuid". So a legitimately tenantless read (an actuator probe,
      a platform-scoped query, a scheduled job before it adopts a tenant) failed with a cast error
      instead of returning nothing.

      NULLIF(..., '') turns the empty string into NULL, and `tenant_id = NULL` is NULL, which is
      not true, so the row is excluded. Same fail-closed outcome, expressed as an answer.

      Behaviour for a tenant-scoped connection is unchanged: a non-empty GUC passes through NULLIF
      untouched and the comparison is exactly what it was.

      Written as a NEW changeset rather than an edit to 011: that one has been applied, and
      Liquibase would see a checksum change. 011 is left as the historical record of what was
      created; this is the record of the correction.

      Fleet note: 40 further policies across auth-service (13), hr-service (19), crm-service (6)
      and file-service (1) still carry the raw-cast form. Both forms in one codebase guarantee the
      wrong one gets copied.
    -->
    <changeSet id="user-1.0.0-013-rls-policy-null-safe-guc" author="restaurantos-agent">
        <sql splitStatements="true" endDelimiter=";">
            DROP POLICY IF EXISTS tenant_isolation ON branches;
            CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON branches
                USING (tenant_id = NULLIF(current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true), '')::uuid);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true" endDelimiter=";">
                DROP POLICY IF EXISTS tenant_isolation ON branches;
                CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON branches
                    USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid);
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
